IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cta-importer`

-- Customs Tariff Act 1995 Schedule 4 -- which goods the Customs By-Laws 2023 prescribe for the items a traveller or small
-- importer meets (items 17, 25, 26, 28, 37), and, for items 26 and 37, whether the concession then applies. A module beside
-- cta-importer.l4 in the same baseline; it IMPORTs that module and changes none of it.
--
-- SEAT: the traveller or small importer (as in cta-importer.l4) -- "I am ordering a $400 jacket from overseas: is it Free?
-- I am importing a used car: which rate applies? I won a trophy abroad: do I pay duty on it?"
--
-- Sources:
--   the Act, Compilation No. 100 (C2026C00399), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A04997.txt, Schedule 4;
--   the Customs By-Laws 2023 (F2023L00366), Compilation No. 6 (F2026C00194, 17 February 2026), made under s 271 of the
--   Customs Act 1901, as deposited at ../../../customs-by-laws-2023/registers/source-bundle/F2023L00366.txt: s 28 (item 17),
--   s 35 (item 25), s 36 (item 26), s 38 (item 28), s 59 (item 37).
--
-- NOT HERE. Item 15 (passengers' goods): the By-Laws 2023 prescribe only item 15(d) (motor vehicles of Canadian and UK forces,
-- s 25); the by-law prescribing the general passenger concession was not found among the instruments deposited (NOTES.md
-- finding 12). The value of goods is the Customs Act's customs value (By-Laws s 5), asked as a fact.

§ `Customs By-Laws 2023 -- which goods Schedule 4 items 17, 25, 26, 28 and 37 cover`

§§ `item 26 -- goods of low value (if you are ordering goods from overseas)`

-- Schedule 4 item 26: "Goods, as prescribed by by-law, whose value is less than the amount prescribed by by-law -- Free".
-- By-Laws s 36(2): "For the purposes of item 26, goods (other than the goods referred to in subsection (3)) the value of which is
-- less than $1000.01 are goods to which that item applies." (3): "Section (2) does not include any of the following goods: (a)
-- tobacco, tobacco products or alcoholic beverages; (a) goods imported by a passenger or a member of the crew of a ship or
-- aircraft arriving in Australia from a place outside Australia; (b) goods forming part of a bulk order." (The compilation
-- prints two paragraphs (a); both are read.)
@export Are my goods "goods of low value" that the Customs By-law prescribes for Schedule 4 item 26?
GIVEN `the customs value of the goods` IS A NUMBER @desc The customs value of the goods, in Australian dollars, as worked out under the Customs Act 1901
      `they are tobacco or alcohol` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the goods are tobacco, tobacco products or alcoholic beverages
      `I bring them in as a passenger or crew` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are bringing the goods in yourself as a passenger, or as a member of the crew, of a ship or aircraft arriving from overseas
      `they are part of a bulk order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the goods form part of a bulk order
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my goods prescribed for item 26` IF
        `the customs value of the goods` LESS THAN 1000.01
    AND (NOT `they are tobacco or alcohol`)
    AND (NOT `I bring them in as a passenger or crew`)
    AND (NOT `they are part of a bulk order`)

@export I am importing goods of low value. Does Schedule 4 item 26 make them Free?
GIVEN `the customs value of the goods` IS A NUMBER @desc The customs value of the goods, in Australian dollars, as worked out under the Customs Act 1901
      `they are tobacco or alcohol` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the goods are tobacco, tobacco products or alcoholic beverages
      `I bring them in as a passenger or crew` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are bringing the goods in yourself as a passenger, or as a member of the crew, of a ship or aircraft arriving from overseas
      `they are part of a bulk order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the goods form part of a bulk order
      `the rate that otherwise applies` IS A NUMBER @desc The rate of duty that would otherwise apply to your goods under Schedule 3 or the free trade schedule that applies, as a percentage (0 for Free)
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Does the concession apply`
`Does item 26 make my low-value goods Free` MEANS
    `Does a concession apply to my goods` `item 26: goods of low value` (`Are my goods prescribed for item 26` `the customs value of the goods` `they are tobacco or alcohol` `I bring them in as a passenger or crew` `they are part of a bulk order`) `the rate that otherwise applies` FALSE

§§ `item 37 -- a used or second-hand passenger car (if you are importing a car)`

-- Schedule 4 item 37: "Used or second-hand passenger motor vehicles, as prescribed by by-law -- 5% (CA: Free)".
-- By-Laws s 59(2): "goods to which that item applies are goods for which both of the following apply: (a) the goods are
-- passenger motor vehicles classified under tariff heading 8703; (b) the goods are either used or second-hand." (3): "subject to
-- the condition that the Minister administering Part 5 of the Road Vehicle Standards Rules 2019 has given, in writing, an
-- import approval ... for the purposes of section 76 of the Road Vehicle Standards Act 2018." (4): "Passenger motor vehicles
-- means motor cars and other motor vehicles (including station wagons) designed for the carriage of 2 or more persons
-- (including the driver), other than: (a) ambulances; (b) hearses; (c) police vans; (d) amphibious vehicles; or (e) off-road
-- vehicles."
@export Is my used car one the Customs By-law prescribes for Schedule 4 item 37?
GIVEN `it is classified under heading 8703` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is classified under tariff heading 8703 (motor cars and other motor vehicles principally designed for the transport of persons)
      `it carries 2 or more people including the driver` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is designed to carry 2 or more people, including the driver
      `it is an ambulance, hearse, police van, amphibious or off-road vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is an ambulance, a hearse, a police van, an amphibious vehicle or an off-road vehicle
      `it is used or second-hand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is used or second-hand
      `I have a written import approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister has given you a written import approval for the vehicle under the Road Vehicle Standards Rules 2019 (for s 76 of the Road Vehicle Standards Act 2018)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my car prescribed for item 37` IF
        `it is classified under heading 8703`
    AND `it carries 2 or more people including the driver`
    AND (NOT `it is an ambulance, hearse, police van, amphibious or off-road vehicle`)
    AND `it is used or second-hand`
    AND `I have a written import approval`

@export I am importing a used car. Does Schedule 4 item 37 give it a lower rate?
GIVEN `it is classified under heading 8703` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is classified under tariff heading 8703 (motor cars and other motor vehicles principally designed for the transport of persons)
      `it carries 2 or more people including the driver` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is designed to carry 2 or more people, including the driver
      `it is an ambulance, hearse, police van, amphibious or off-road vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is an ambulance, a hearse, a police van, an amphibious vehicle or an off-road vehicle
      `it is used or second-hand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is used or second-hand
      `I have a written import approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister has given you a written import approval for the vehicle under the Road Vehicle Standards Rules 2019 (for s 76 of the Road Vehicle Standards Act 2018)
      `the rate that otherwise applies` IS A NUMBER @desc The rate of duty that would otherwise apply to the car under Schedule 3 or the free trade schedule that applies, as a percentage (0 for Free)
      `the car is the produce of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the car is the produce or manufacture of Canada
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Does the concession apply`
`Does item 37 apply to my used car` MEANS
    `Does a concession apply to my goods` `item 37: a used or second-hand passenger car` (`Is my car prescribed for item 37` `it is classified under heading 8703` `it carries 2 or more people including the driver` `it is an ambulance, hearse, police van, amphibious or off-road vehicle` `it is used or second-hand` `I have a written import approval`) `the rate that otherwise applies` `the car is the produce of Canada`

§§ `item 25 -- a trophy, decoration, medallion, certificate or prize from overseas (if you won or were sent one)`

-- Schedule 4 item 25: "Goods, as prescribed by by-law, that are: (a) trophies won outside Australia; or (b) decorations,
-- medallions or certificates awarded outside Australia; or (c) trophies or prizes sent by donors resident outside Australia for
-- presentation or competition in Australia -- Free".
-- By-Laws s 35(2): "For the purposes of paragraph (a) of item 25, each of the following are goods to which that paragraph of the
-- item applies: (a) the goods are trophies won outside of Australia in competition; and (b) the trophies are appliances or
-- articles of a kind used in an office or the household." Read with its "and", both must hold (NOTES.md finding 11).
-- (3): "decorations, medallions or certificates awarded outside of Australia". (4): for paragraph (c), "(a) the goods are
-- trophies or prizes sent by donors resident outside Australia; and (b) the goods were sent either: (i) for presentation in
-- Australia; or (ii) for competitions in Australia organised or sponsored otherwise than in connection with commercial
-- ventures; and (c) the goods are of a kind which are suitable for display on: (i) walls of dwellings or offices; or (ii)
-- stands or similar mounts; or (iii) the person." (5): "subject to the condition that those goods are not of an advertising
-- nature."
DECLARE `What my award is` IS ONE OF
    `a trophy I won in a competition outside Australia`
    `a decoration, medallion or certificate awarded to me outside Australia`
    `a trophy or prize sent by a donor living outside Australia`
    `something else`

@export Is my trophy, decoration, medallion, certificate or prize one the Customs By-law prescribes for Schedule 4 item 25 (so that it is Free)?
GIVEN `what it is` IS A `What my award is` @desc What the goods are: a trophy you won in a competition overseas, a decoration, medallion or certificate awarded overseas, a trophy or prize sent by a donor living overseas, or something else
      `it is an article of a kind used in an office or household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a trophy won overseas: whether it is an appliance or article of a kind used in an office or the household
      `it was sent for presentation or a non-commercial competition here` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a trophy or prize from an overseas donor: whether it was sent for presentation in Australia, or for a competition in Australia not organised or sponsored in connection with a commercial venture
      `it is for display on a wall, a stand or the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a trophy or prize from an overseas donor: whether it is of a kind suitable for display on the walls of a home or office, on a stand or similar mount, or on the person
      `it is of an advertising nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the goods are of an advertising nature
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my award prescribed for item 25` IF
        (NOT `it is of an advertising nature`)
    AND (CONSIDER `what it is`
         WHEN `a trophy I won in a competition outside Australia` THEN `it is an article of a kind used in an office or household`
         WHEN `a decoration, medallion or certificate awarded to me outside Australia` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a trophy or prize sent by a donor living outside Australia` THEN `it was sent for presentation or a non-commercial competition here` AND `it is for display on a wall, a stand or the person`
         WHEN `something else` THEN FALSE)

§§ `item 28 -- an aid or appliance for a person with a disability`

-- Schedule 4 item 28: "Aids and appliances, as prescribed by by-law, for persons with disabilities -- Free".
-- By-Laws s 38(2): "(a) goods that are pedestrian safety equipment and are either: (i) braille tiles; or (ii) braille road
-- rivets; (b) goods that are reading machines and are capable of converting printed matter into either: (i) tactile images;
-- or (ii) speech; (c) goods that are reading systems and that are capable of scanning printed matter and reproducing the
-- enlarged text on a screen; (d) goods that are sound reproducers and sound recorders." (3): (a) goods "designed for the
-- blind". (4): (d) goods must "(a) have a power output (rms) of less than 2.5 W; (b) use a magnetic tape as the recorded or
-- recording medium; (c) are monophonic; (d) are DC or AC/DC operated; (e) are designed for carrying in the hand or on the
-- person; (f) have colour coded, raised symbol control keys; (g) have dual playing speeds."
DECLARE `What my aid is` IS ONE OF
    `braille tiles or braille road rivets (pedestrian safety equipment)`
    `a reading machine that converts print into tactile images or speech`
    `a reading system that scans print and shows it enlarged on a screen`
    `a sound reproducer and recorder`
    `another aid or appliance`

@export Is my aid or appliance for a person with a disability one the Customs By-law prescribes for Schedule 4 item 28 (so that it is Free)?
GIVEN `what it is` IS A `What my aid is` @desc What the goods are
      `it is designed for the blind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For braille tiles or road rivets: whether they are designed for the blind
      `power output under 2.5 W rms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a sound reproducer and recorder: whether its power output (rms) is less than 2.5 W
      `it uses magnetic tape` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a sound reproducer and recorder: whether it uses magnetic tape as the recorded or recording medium
      `it is monophonic` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a sound reproducer and recorder: whether it is monophonic
      `it is DC or AC/DC operated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a sound reproducer and recorder: whether it is DC or AC/DC operated
      `it is designed to be carried` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a sound reproducer and recorder: whether it is designed for carrying in the hand or on the person
      `it has colour coded raised control keys` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a sound reproducer and recorder: whether it has colour coded, raised symbol control keys
      `it has dual playing speeds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a sound reproducer and recorder: whether it has dual playing speeds
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my aid prescribed for item 28` IF
    CONSIDER `what it is`
    WHEN `braille tiles or braille road rivets (pedestrian safety equipment)` THEN `it is designed for the blind`
    WHEN `a reading machine that converts print into tactile images or speech` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a reading system that scans print and shows it enlarged on a screen` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a sound reproducer and recorder` THEN
            `power output under 2.5 W rms`
        AND `it uses magnetic tape`
        AND `it is monophonic`
        AND `it is DC or AC/DC operated`
        AND `it is designed to be carried`
        AND `it has colour coded raised control keys`
        AND `it has dual playing speeds`
    WHEN `another aid or appliance` THEN FALSE

§§ `item 17 -- goods I exported and brought back (if you are bringing back goods taken out of Australia)`

-- Schedule 4 item 17: goods, "as prescribed by by-law", exported and returned without treatment since, and not item 17A goods.
-- By-Laws s 28(2): "goods that were exported from Australia, on a temporary basis, to the Australian Antarctic Territory, or the
-- Territory of Heard Island and McDonald Islands, are goods to which that item applies"; (3): "(a) the goods are returned and
-- have not been subject to any treatment, repair, renovation, alteration or any other process since their export; (b) item 17A
-- ... does not apply to the goods." Goods exported anywhere else are not prescribed by the By-Laws 2023 (NOTES.md finding 13).
DECLARE `Where my goods went` IS ONE OF
    `the Australian Antarctic Territory, or Heard Island and McDonald Islands`
    `somewhere else`

@export I am bringing back goods I took out of Australia. Are they prescribed for Schedule 4 item 17 by the Customs By-Laws 2023 (so that they are Free)?
GIVEN `where they went` IS A `Where my goods went` @desc Where the goods were exported to
      `they went on a temporary basis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they were exported on a temporary basis
      `they are unaltered since export` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they have had no treatment, repair, renovation, alteration or other process since they were exported
      `item 17A applies to them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Schedule 4 item 17A applies to them
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my returned goods prescribed for item 17` IF
        `where they went` EQUALS `the Australian Antarctic Territory, or Heard Island and McDonald Islands`
    AND `they went on a temporary basis`
    AND `they are unaltered since export`
    AND (NOT `item 17A applies to them`)
